# Normalize line endings. Shell scripts MUST stay LF so bash works in WSL.
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf

# The frozen baseline is verified byte-for-byte against the SHA-256 hashes in its MANIFEST.json.
# Under `text=auto` git would store LF and hand back CRLF on Windows but LF on Linux/Colab, so a
# clone on the other platform would fail every hash while the data was in fact untouched. Stored
# verbatim instead: these files are a record, not source. See docs/improvements.md §3.
artifacts/baseline/** -text
